17:06.293 --> 17:17.541
[SPEAKER_00]: profile kite. Yeah, totally. There was such a huge step from those speed wings to this kite. You can't imagine. It's like going from an A-wing to

17:17.681 --> 17:29.552
[SPEAKER_01]: probably like a competition hang glider kind of thing. Wow. It's just unreal, you know? And then I hear that. I mean, just for the perspective

17:29.592 --> 17:38.339
[SPEAKER_00]: of our listeners, you basically attach the kite risers on carabiners, and those carabiners were attached to a paragliding harness, and that

17:38.379 --> 17:47.766
[SPEAKER_00]: was your setup when you were having fun. Exactly, yeah. Wow. Do they have those kind of riders? Is it possible to fit in a paragliding harness? Can

17:47.786 --> 17:57.791
[SPEAKER_00]: you put a board harness and a kite and kind of make it work? Yeah, it actually works pretty simple. Amazingly simple it works, yeah. Yeah,

17:58.352 --> 18:06.297
[SPEAKER_01]: but it's still a kite, you know, and if this thing does collapse, it might not reopen, you know, so as long as you don't fly, you know, higher than

